digraph ReasoningTree {
  rankdir="TB";
  "N10" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction-rule: If a technology can convert dissolved carbon using only sunlight, then it offers an energy-efficient solution."];
  "N12" [label="(23,1,0) Abduction-phenomenon: Conventional PEC devices have low STF efficiency (0.08-0.63%)."];
  "N13" [label="(17,1,0) Abduction-knowledge: pH gradient, ion transport, and acid-base buffer reactions are major transport losses."];
  "N15" [label="(15,2,0) Deduction-case: In static PEC devices, diffusion is the dominant transport mechanism."];
  "N16" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction-rule: If diffusion dominates transport in buffered electrolyte, then pH gradients form between electrodes."];
  "N2" [label="(2,1,0) Direct air capture is energy-intensive."];
  "N21" [label="(34,1,0) Abduction-phenomenon: Continuous CO2-OH- reaction depletes CO2(aq) to near zero."];
  "N22" [label="(34,2,0) Abduction-knowledge: CO2(aq) depletion eliminates selectivity for carbon products."];
  "N3" [label="(2,2,0) Direct air capture is costly."];
  "N31" [label="(41,1,0) Abduction-phenomenon: CO2 bubbling schemes are impractical to scale for large-area ocean PEC reactors."];
  "N32" [label="(0,0,0) Abduction-knowledge: Ocean-based systems need to operate without external CO2 supply."];
  "N34" [label="(11,1,0) Deduction-case: Integrated PEC process for direct utilization consumes less energy than stepwise approach."];
  "N35" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction-rule: If an integrated process consumes less energy, then it is more economically viable."];
  "N37" [label="(44,1,0) Abduction-phenomenon: Flow can replace diffusion to dominate transport."];
  "N38" [label="(0,0,0) Abduction-knowledge: Boundary layer flow confines reactant flux near surfaces and reduces pH gradients."];
  "N40" [label="(52,1,0) Deduction-case: Boundary-layer shear flow confines continuous CO2(aq) flux from photoanode to photocathode."];
  "N41" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction-rule: If CO2(aq) flux is confined near cathode surface, then sufficient reactant is maintained for CO2R."];
  "N43" [label="(53,1,0) Abduction-phenomenon: BiVO4 photoanode generates H+ to acidify HCO3- in flowing seawater."];
  "N44" [label="(6,2,0) Abduction-knowledge: Bicarbonate acidification generates dissolved CO2 via HCO3- + H+ → CO2(aq) + H2O."];
  "N46" [label="(54,1,0) Deduction-case: Flow prevents out-diffusion of CO2(aq) to bulk seawater."];
  "N47" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction-rule: If out-diffusion is prevented, then transport flux increases and residence time decreases."];
  "N49" [label="(55,1,0) Abduction-phenomenon: Flow energy can be harvested from tidal waves and ocean currents."];
  "N50" [label="(0,0,0) Abduction-knowledge: Renewable flow energy makes boundary layer flow scheme practical for ocean deployment."];
  "N52" [label="(58,1,0) Deduction-case: Boundary layer flow reduces pH gradient and concentration-limited transport losses."];
  "N53" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction-rule: If pH gradient and transport losses are reduced, then PEC device efficiency improves."];
  "N9" [label="(5,1,0) Deduction-case: Conversion of dissolved carbon in seawater can be entirely powered by sunlight using PEC devices."];
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) Develop and evaluate a sunlight-powered photoelectrochemical molecular flux catalysis strategy that uses boundary-layer shear flow in a BiVO4 photoanode–photocathode seawater device to acidify bicarbonate in situ, direct CO2(aq) flux to catalysts, reduce pH-gradient and transport losses, avoid external CO2 bubbling, and improve carbon-product selectivity and solar-to-fuel efficiency.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) When seawater carbon availability, PEC transport limitations, boundary-layer-flow mechanisms, and measured efficiency/selectivity improvements all point to the same bottleneck and solution, they jointly motivate developing and evaluating an integrated molecular-flux PEC device for direct seawater carbon conversion."];
  "R10" [label="(0,0,0) Continuous CO2-OH- reaction and CO2(aq) depletion explain why static devices struggle to maintain selectivity for carbon products."];
  "R12" [label="(0,0,0) Large-area ocean PEC reactors motivate an integrated approach that can operate without external CO2 bubbling."];
  "R13" [label="(0,0,0) An integrated PEC process for direct utilization is more economically viable than a stepwise approach when it consumes less energy."];
  "R14" [label="(0,0,0) Boundary-layer flow is a plausible transport strategy for addressing diffusion-related limitations because it can dominate transport, confine reactant flux near surfaces, and reduce pH gradients."];
  "R15" [label="(0,0,0) Boundary-layer shear flow can maintain sufficient CO2R reactant near the cathode by confining continuous CO2(aq) flux from the photoanode to the photocathode."];
  "R16" [label="(0,0,0) A BiVO4 photoanode can generate H+ that acidifies bicarbonate in flowing seawater to produce dissolved CO2 in situ."];
  "R17" [label="(0,0,0) Flow can enhance CO2(aq) utilization by preventing out-diffusion to bulk seawater, increasing transport flux and decreasing residence time."];
  "R18" [label="(0,0,0) Ocean-based boundary-layer-flow operation is feasible in principle because flow energy can be harvested from tidal waves and ocean currents."];
  "R19" [label="(0,0,0) A boundary-layer-flow PEC device is expected to achieve higher efficiency when the flow reduces pH gradients and concentration-limited transport losses."];
  "R21" [label="(0,0,0) Molecular flux catalysis with boundary-layer flow can enable continuous CO2(aq) flux near catalyst surfaces while reducing pH-gradient limitations."];
  "R4" [label="(0,0,0) The energy intensity and cost of direct air capture motivate exploring alternative CO2 sources."];
  "R6" [label="(0,0,0) PEC devices offer an energy-efficient route for dissolved carbon conversion when that conversion can be powered entirely by sunlight."];
  "R7" [label="(0,0,0) Conventional PEC performance suggests that transport losses, including pH gradients, are important limitations for diffusion-based seawater CO2 conversion."];
  "R8" [label="(0,0,0) Static PEC devices in buffered electrolyte are expected to form pH gradients because diffusion dominates their transport."];
